```javascript
function arraySum(arr) {
  if (arr.length === 0) {
    return 0;
  }

  const [first, ...rest] = arr;
  return first + arraySum(rest);
}
```

This function uses destructuring assignment to extract the first element of the array (`first`) and create a new array (`rest`) with the remaining elements. It then recursively calls `arraySum` on the `rest` array, and adds the `first` element to the result.

