The `is_prime(num)` function iterates from 2 to the square root of `num` and checks if `num` is divisible by any number in this range. If it is, the function returns `False`, indicating that the number is not prime. Otherwise, it returns `True`.

The `sum_prime_factors(num)` function finds all prime factors of `num` by iterating from 2 to the square root of `num` and checking if `num` is divisible by each number in this range. If a number is a prime factor, it is added to a list. Finally, the function returns the sum of the prime factors.

