Here's a Java program that solves cubic equations with complex roots, handling both real and complex coefficients:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class CubicEquationSolver {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.println("Enter the coefficients of the cubic equation:");
        System.out.print("a: ");
        double a = scanner.nextDouble();
        System.out.print("b: ");
        double b = scanner.nextDouble();
        System.out.print("c: ");
        double c = scanner.nextDouble();
        System.out.print("d: ");
        double d = scanner.nextDouble();

        solveCubicEquation(a, b, c, d);

        scanner.close();
    }

    public static void solveCubicEquation(double a, double b, double c, double d) {
        if (a == 0) {
            System.out.println("Not a cubic equation!");
            return;
        }

        double delta0 = b * b - 3 * a * c;
        double delta1 = 2 * b * b * b - 9 * a * b * c + 27 * a * a * d;
        double C = Math.pow((delta1 + Math.sqrt(delta1 * delta1 - 4 * delta0 * delta0 * delta0)) / 2, 1.0 / 3.0);

        if (delta0 == 0 && delta1 == 0) {
            System.out.println("All three roots are real and equal:");
            double x1 = -b / (3 * a);
            System.out.println("x1 = " + x1);
        } else if (delta0 > 0) {
            double y1 = ((delta1 + Math.sqrt(delta1 * delta1 - 4 * delta0 * delta0 * delta0)) / 2);
            double y2 = ((delta1 - Math.sqrt(delta1 * delta1 - 4 * delta0 * delta0 * delta0)) / 2);
            double C1 = Math.pow(y1, 1.0 / 3.0);
            double C2 = Math.pow(y2, 1.0 / 3.0);

            double x1 = (-1 / (3 * a)) * (b + C + delta0 / C);
            double x2 = (-1 / (3 * a)) * (b + (C1 + C2) / -2 + (C1 - C2) * Math.sqrt(3) / 2);
            double x3 = (-1 / (3 * a)) * (b + (C1 + C2) / -2 - (C1 - C2) * Math.sqrt(3) / 2);

            System.out.println("Three real roots:");
            System.out.println("x1 = " + x1);
            System.out.println("x2 = " + x2);
            System.out.println("x3 = " + x3);
        } else if (delta0 < 0) {
            double C3 = Math.pow(-delta0 / 2, 1.0 / 3.0);
            double C4 = Math.acos(delta1 / (2 * delta0 * Math.sqrt(-delta0)));

            double x1 = (-1 / (3 * a)) * (b + 2 * C3 * Math.cos(C4 / 3));
            double x2 = (-1 / (3 * a)) * (b + 2 * C3 * Math.cos((C4 + 2 * Math.PI) / 3));
            double x3 = (-1 / (3 * a)) * (b + 2 * C3 * Math.cos((C4 + 4 * Math.PI) / 3));

            System.out.println("One real root and two complex roots:");
            System.out.println("x1 = " + x1);
            System.out.println("x2 = " + x2 + " + " + (Math.sqrt(3) * Math.abs(x3)) + "i");
            System.out.println("x3 = " + x2 + " - " + (Math.sqrt(3) * Math.abs(x3)) + "i");
        }
    }
}
```

This program prompts the user to enter the coefficients of the cubic equation and then calls the `solveCubicEquation` method to solve it. The `solveCubicEquation` method applies the cubic formula to find the roots of the equation. The program handles three cases: when all three roots are real and equal, when all three roots are real and different, and when one root is real and the other two are complex conjugates. The roots are then printed to the console.

