- The `IndexOf` method is called with the `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` parameter to ignore the case of the letters. This means that the search will be case-insensitive.
- If the `IndexOf` method returns a non-negative value (indicating that the substring was found), the method returns `true`. Otherwise, it returns `false`.

