```java
public static String convertToUpperCase(String input) {
    StringBuilder output = new StringBuilder();
    for (int i = 0; i < input.length(); i++) {
        char c = input.charAt(i);
        if (Character.isLowerCase(c)) {
            output.append(Character.toUpperCase(c));
        } else {
            output.append(c);
        }
    }
    return output.toString();
}
```

In this function, we use a `StringBuilder` to build the uppercase version of the input string. We iterate over each character in the input string using a `for` loop and use the `Character.isLowerCase()` method to check if the character is lowercase. If it is, we use the `Character.toUpperCase()` method to convert it to uppercase and append it to the `StringBuilder`. If the character is already uppercase or is not a letter, we simply append it as it is. Finally, we convert the `StringBuilder` to a string using the `toString()` method and return it.

