class CustomClass implements Comparable<CustomClass>, Serializable, Cloneable {
    private String attribute1;
    private Integer attribute2;

    public CustomClass(String attribute1, Integer attribute2) {
        this.attribute1 = attribute1;
        this.attribute2 = attribute2;
    }

    public String getAttribute1() {
        return attribute1;
    }

    public Integer getAttribute2() {
        return attribute2;
    }

    @Override
    public int compareTo(CustomClass other) {
        // Handle null values for attribute1
        if (this.attribute1 == null && other.attribute1 != null) {
            return 1;
        } else if (this.attribute1 != null && other.attribute1 == null) {
            return -1;
        } else if (this.attribute1 == null && other.attribute1 == null) {
            // If both attribute1 are null, sort based on attribute2
            return this.attribute2.compareTo(other.attribute2);
        }

        // Compare attribute1 values
        int result = this.attribute1.compareTo(other.attribute1);

        // If attribute1 values are the same, compare attribute2 values
        if (result == 0) {
            result = this.attribute2.compareTo(other.attribute2);
        }

        return result;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if (this == obj) {
            return true;
        }
        if (obj == null || getClass() != obj.getClass()) {
            return false;
        }

        CustomClass other = (CustomClass) obj;

        if (attribute1 != null ? !attribute1.equals(other.attribute1) : other.attribute1 != null) {
            return false;
        }
        return attribute2 != null ? attribute2.equals(other.attribute2) : other.attribute2 == null;
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        int result = attribute1 != null ? attribute1.hashCode() : 0;
        result = 31 * result + (attribute2 != null ? attribute2.hashCode() : 0);
        return result;
    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return "CustomClass{" +
                "attribute1='" + attribute1 + '\'' +
                ", attribute2=" + attribute2 +
                '}';
    }

    // Other required methods for Serializable or Cloneable interfaces
    // ...

}

public class CustomClassSorter {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<CustomClass> customList = new ArrayList<>();
        customList.add(new CustomClass("foo", 2));
        customList.add(new CustomClass("bar", 1));
        customList.add(new CustomClass(null, 3));
        customList.add(new CustomClass("baz", null));
        customList.add(new CustomClass(null, null));

        customList = customSort(customList);

        for (CustomClass customObj : customList) {
            System.out.println(customObj);
        }
    }

    public static List<CustomClass> customSort(List<CustomClass> customList) {
        if (customList.size() <= 1) {
            return customList;
        }

        int middle = customList.size() / 2;
        List<CustomClass> leftList = customSort(customList.subList(0, middle));
        List<CustomClass> rightList = customSort(customList.subList(middle, customList.size()));

        return merge(leftList, rightList);
    }

    public static List<CustomClass> merge(List<CustomClass> leftList, List<CustomClass> rightList) {
        List<CustomClass> mergedList = new ArrayList<>();
        int leftIndex = 0;
        int rightIndex = 0;

        while (leftIndex < leftList.size() && rightIndex < rightList.size()) {
            CustomClass leftObj = leftList.get(leftIndex);
            CustomClass rightObj = rightList.get(rightIndex);

            if (leftObj.compareTo(rightObj) <= 0) {
                mergedList.add(leftObj);
                leftIndex++;
            } else {
                mergedList.add(rightObj);
                rightIndex++;
            }
        }

        mergedList.addAll(leftList.subList(leftIndex, leftList.size()));
        mergedList.addAll(rightList.subList(rightIndex, rightList.size()));

        return mergedList;
    }
}
```

This code implements a `CustomClass` with two attributes (`attribute1` and `attribute2`) and a constructor to initialize them. The `CustomClass` also implements the `Comparable` interface and overrides the `compareTo()` method to define the sorting logic based on the attributes.

The `CustomClass` also implements the `Serializable` and `Cloneable` interfaces and overrides the required methods (`equals()`, `hashCode()`, `toString()`, and other required methods for the interfaces).

The code also handles cases where the specific attribute (`attribute1`) is null for some objects in the list. Objects with null values for `attribute1` are placed at the end of the sorted list. If there are multiple objects with null values, they are sorted among themselves based on `attribute2`.

Instead of using the built-in sorting algorithm, the code implements a custom sorting algorithm called Merge Sort. The `customSort()` method recursively divides the list into two halves until each sublist has only one element. Then, the `merge()` method merges the sorted sublists in ascending order based on the defined sorting logic. The custom sorting algorithm has a time complexity of O(n log n).

