Here's an example implementation of a PHP function that checks if a given string starts with a given substring, is case-sensitive, and also checks if the substring appears in the middle of any word in the string. It also ignores whitespace characters at the beginning or end of the string.

```php
function startsWithSubstring($string, $substring) {
    // Remove whitespace from the beginning and end of the string
    $trimmedString = trim($string);

    // Get the length of the substring and string
    $substringLength = strlen($substring);
    $stringLength = strlen($trimmedString);

    // Check if the string is shorter than the substring
    if ($stringLength < $substringLength) {
        return false;
    }

    // Iterate through each character in the substring and string
    for ($i = 0; $i < $substringLength; $i++) {
        // Check if the characters are different
        if ($trimmedString[$i] !== $substring[$i]) {
            return false;
        }
    }

    // Check if the substring appears in the middle of any word
    if ($stringLength > $substringLength && !ctype_space($trimmedString[$substringLength])) {
        return false;
    }

    return true;
}
```

