Here is a JavaScript function that determines if an array is sorted in non-decreasing order or not, with a time complexity of O(n):

```javascript
function isSorted(arr) {
  for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] < arr[i - 1]) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

In this function, we iterate over the array starting from index 1 and compare each element with the previous element. If we find an element that is less than the previous element, it means the array is not sorted in non-decreasing order, so we return false. If we reach the end of the loop without finding any out-of-order elements, it means the array is sorted in non-decreasing order, so we return true.

The time complexity of this function is O(n) because we only need to iterate through the array once.

