Here is the Java function that checks if a given string is a palindrome while ignoring punctuation marks and white spaces. It also returns the count of distinct characters in the string:

```java
public class PalindromeChecker {

    public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
        // Remove punctuation marks and white spaces from the string
        String cleanString = str.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z]", "");

        // Convert the string to lowercase
        String lowerCaseString = cleanString.toLowerCase();

        // Check if the string is a palindrome
        int length = lowerCaseString.length();
        for (int i = 0; i < length / 2; i++) {
            if (lowerCaseString.charAt(i) != lowerCaseString.charAt(length - 1 - i)) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }

    public static int countDistinctCharacters(String str) {
        // Remove white spaces from the string
        String cleanString = str.replaceAll("\\s", "");

        // Create a set to store distinct characters
        Set<Character> distinctCharacters = new HashSet<>();

        // Add each character to the set
        for (char c : cleanString.toCharArray()) {
            distinctCharacters.add(c);
        }

        // Return the count of distinct characters
        return distinctCharacters.size();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "A man, a plan, a canal: Panama!";

        if (isPalindrome(input)) {
            System.out.println("The string is a palindrome.");
        } else {
            System.out.println("The string is not a palindrome.");
        }

        int distinctCount = countDistinctCharacters(input);
        System.out.println("The count of distinct characters is: " + distinctCount);
    }
}
```

In this example, the `isPalindrome` function checks if the input string is a palindrome by comparing the characters from the beginning and end of the string. It ignores punctuation marks and converts all characters to lowercase to ensure case-sensitivity.

The `countDistinctCharacters` function removes white spaces from the string and creates a set to store distinct characters. It iterates through each character in the string and adds it to the set. Finally, it returns the size of the set, which represents the count of distinct characters in the string.

