Here's an example Java program that clones an array of objects implementing the "Cloneable" interface:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;

interface Cloneable {
    Cloneable clone();
}

class MyClass implements Cloneable {
    private int value;

    public MyClass(int value) {
        this.value = value;
    }

    public int getValue() {
        return value;
    }

    public void setValue(int value) {
        this.value = value;
    }

    @Override
    public Cloneable clone() {
        return new MyClass(value);
    }
}

public class ArrayCloner {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        MyClass[] originalArray = {new MyClass(1), new MyClass(2), new MyClass(3)};

        MyClass[] clonedArray = cloneArray(originalArray);

        // Modify the cloned array
        clonedArray[0].setValue(10);

        // Print the original array
        System.out.println("Original Array:");
        for (MyClass obj : originalArray) {
            System.out.println(obj.getValue());
        }

        // Print the cloned array
        System.out.println("Cloned Array:");
        for (MyClass obj : clonedArray) {
            System.out.println(obj.getValue());
        }
    }

    public static <T extends Cloneable> T[] cloneArray(T[] array) {
        return Arrays.stream(array)
                .map(item -> (T) item.clone())
                .toArray(size -> Arrays.copyOf(array, size));
    }
}
```

In this program, we have an interface called `Cloneable` that defines a `clone()` method. The `MyClass` class implements this interface and provides its own implementation of the `clone()` method.

The `ArrayCloner` class demonstrates how to clone an array of objects implementing the `Cloneable` interface. The `cloneArray()` method uses Java streams to iterate over each object in the original array, calls the `clone()` method on each object, and collects the cloned objects into a new array. Note that we need to cast the cloned object back to the type `T`.

Finally, the `main()` method creates an array of `MyClass` objects, clones the array using the `cloneArray()` method, modifies an element in the cloned array, and prints both the original and cloned arrays to demonstrate that they are independent of each other.

