2. If the exponent is negative, we calculate the reciprocal of the result for a positive exponent.
3. If the exponent is even, we calculate the result by squaring the base and halving the exponent.
4. If the exponent is odd, we calculate the result by multiplying the base with the result of squaring the base and subtracting 1 from the exponent before halving it.

This algorithm takes advantage of the fact that any number raised to an even exponent can be expressed as the square of that number raised to half the exponent. By recursively applying this property, we can calculate the result with a time complexity of O(log n).

