console.log(sortArray(arr)); // Output: [-2, -8, -4, -1, -6, 5, 10, 7, 3]
```

This script uses a two-pointer approach. The pointer `i` starts from the beginning of the array and moves towards the end, while the pointer `j` starts from the end and moves towards the beginning. The script swaps positive numbers with negative numbers when necessary, and increments or decrements the pointers accordingly. This continues until `i` is greater than `j`, at which point the array is sorted.

