        list.add(10);
        list.add(20);
        list.add(30);
        list.add(40);
        list.add(50);

        System.out.println("\nList elements:");
        for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) {
            System.out.println(list.get(i));
        }
    }
}
```

In the above code, an array of integers is created with a fixed size of 5. Each element is assigned a value using indices. In contrast, an ArrayList (a type of list) is created without specifying a size. Elements are added using the `add()` method.

