To improve the efficiency of the function and avoid using built-in string manipulation functions, we can iterate over each character in the input string `x` and check if it is uppercase or lowercase. If it is uppercase, we will convert it to lowercase and append it to a new string. If it is lowercase, we will convert it to uppercase and append it to the new string. Finally, we will return the new string.

Here is the updated function:

```python
def swap_case(x: str) -> str:
    result = ""
    for char in x:
        if char.isupper():
            result += chr(ord(char) + 32)  # Convert uppercase to lowercase
        elif char.islower():
            result += chr(ord(char) - 32)  # Convert lowercase to uppercase
        else:
            result += char  # Keep non-alphabetic characters unchanged
    return result
```

This implementation has a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the input string `x`.

