Here is a Java program that solves the Tower of Hanoi puzzle and calculates the minimum number of moves needed. It also allows the user to input the number of disks in the puzzle.

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class TowerOfHanoi {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the number of disks (minimum 3, maximum 10): ");
        int numDisks = scanner.nextInt();

        if (numDisks < 3 || numDisks > 10) {
            System.out.println("Invalid number of disks. Please try again.");
            return;
        }

        int moves = solveTowerOfHanoi(numDisks, 'A', 'C', 'B');
        System.out.println("Minimum number of moves: " + moves);
    }

    public static int solveTowerOfHanoi(int numDisks, char source, char destination, char auxiliary) {
        if (numDisks == 1) {
            System.out.println("Move disk 1 from " + source + " to " + destination);
            return 1;
        }

        int moves = solveTowerOfHanoi(numDisks - 1, source, auxiliary, destination);
        System.out.println("Move disk " + numDisks + " from " + source + " to " + destination);
        moves++;
        moves += solveTowerOfHanoi(numDisks - 1, auxiliary, destination, source);

        return moves;
    }
}
```

This program uses a recursive approach to solve the Tower of Hanoi puzzle. The `solveTowerOfHanoi` method takes the number of disks, source tower, destination tower, and auxiliary tower as parameters. It recursively solves the subproblem of moving `numDisks - 1` disks from the source tower to the auxiliary tower, then moves the last disk from the source tower to the destination tower, and finally solves the subproblem of moving the `numDisks - 1` disks from the auxiliary tower to the destination tower. The base case is when there is only one disk, which is directly moved from the source tower to the destination tower.

The program also checks if the user enters a valid number of disks (between 3 and 10) before solving the puzzle. If an invalid number is entered, an error message is displayed and the program exits.

