Here's the modified program that sorts the given array in descending order using bubble sort algorithm:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] array = {16, 5, 1, 8, 10};

        bubbleSortDescending(array);

        System.out.println("Sorted array in descending order:");
        for (int num : array) {
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
    }

    public static void bubbleSortDescending(int[] array) {
        int n = array.length;

        for (int i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++) {
                if (array[j] < array[j+1]) {
                    // swap array[j] and array[j+1]
                    int temp = array[j];
                    array[j] = array[j+1];
                    array[j+1] = temp;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Output:
```
Sorted array in descending order:
16 10 8 5 1
```

This program implements the bubble sort algorithm which compares adjacent elements in the array and swaps them if they are in the wrong order. The inner loop runs for `n-i-1` times for each outer loop iteration, where `n` is the length of the array and `i` is the current outer loop index. This results in a time complexity of O(n^2) as required.

