```cpp
#include <vector>

std::vector<int> findAsciiValues(const std::string& str) {
    std::vector<int> asciiValues;
    bool foundNonSpace = false;
    int i = 0;

    // Ignore leading white spaces
    while (str[i] == ' ') {
        i++;
    }

    // Traverse the string and find ASCII values of non-space characters
    while (i < str.length()) {
        if (str[i] != ' ') {
            foundNonSpace = true;
            asciiValues.push_back(static_cast<int>(str[i]));
        }
        i++;
    }

    // Ignore trailing white spaces
    if (!foundNonSpace) {
        return asciiValues;  // No non-space characters found
    }

    while (asciiValues.back() == ' ') {
        asciiValues.pop_back();
    }

    return asciiValues;
}
```

Explanation:
- The function takes a constant reference to a string as input.
- It initializes an empty vector `asciiValues` to store the ASCII values of non-space characters.
- It also initializes a boolean variable `foundNonSpace` to keep track of whether any non-space characters have been found.
- The function then ignores any leading white spaces by incrementing `i` until `str[i]` is not a space character.
- Next, it traverses the string starting from the position `i` and checks if each character is a space or not.
- If a non-space character is found, `foundNonSpace` is set to true and its ASCII value is added to `asciiValues` using the `push_back()` function.
- After the traversal, the function checks if any non-space characters were found. If not, it immediately returns an empty `asciiValues` vector.
- Finally, it ignores any trailing white spaces in `asciiValues` by repeatedly using the `pop_back()` function until the last element is not a space character.
- The function then returns the `asciiValues` vector containing the ASCII values of non-space characters in the input string.

Note: The function assumes that the input string contains only ASCII characters. If the input string can contain Unicode or other non-ASCII characters, the function needs to be modified accordingly.

