The formula to calculate the total cost of an item, given the item price, tax rate, and any applicable discounts or surcharges, along with multiple discount tiers based on the total quantity of items purchased, is as follows:

Total Cost = (Item Price * Quantity) * (1 - Discount Rate) * (1 + Tax Rate)

Where:
- Item Price is the price of a single item.
- Quantity is the total quantity of items purchased.
- Discount Rate is the applicable discount rate based on the total quantity of items purchased.
- Tax Rate is the tax rate applied to the item price.

To implement the discount tiers based on the total quantity of items purchased, you can use the following logic:

