    Discount Rate = 0.10;
} else if (Quantity > 20) {
    Discount Rate = 0.15;
} else {
    Discount Rate = 0; // No discount applied
}

Now, you can use this logic in the formula to calculate the total cost. Here's an example of how you can implement this in a programming language like Python:

def calculate_total_cost(item_price, tax_rate, quantity):
    if quantity >= 1 and quantity <= 10:
        discount_rate = 0.05
    elif quantity >= 11 and quantity <= 20:
        discount_rate = 0.10
    elif quantity > 20:
        discount_rate = 0.15
    else:
        discount_rate = 0

    total_cost = (item_price * quantity) * (1 - discount_rate) * (1 + tax_rate)
    return total_cost

