Here is an example Java program that counts the frequency of a given word in a sentence, considering the requirements specified:

```java
import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;

public class WordFrequencyCounter {

    public static int countWordFrequency(String sentence, String word) {
        // Remove leading and trailing whitespace from sentence and word
        sentence = sentence.trim();
        word = word.trim();

        // Remove HTML tags and attributes from the sentence
        sentence = removeHtmlTags(sentence);

        // Prepare the regex pattern to find the word as a separate word
        String pattern = "\\b" + Pattern.quote(word) + "\\b";
        Pattern wordPattern = Pattern.compile(pattern, Pattern.CASE_INSENSITIVE);

        // Count the frequency of the word
        int frequency = 0;
        Matcher matcher = wordPattern.matcher(sentence);
        while (matcher.find()) {
            frequency++;
        }

        return frequency;
    }

    private static String removeHtmlTags(String sentence) {
        // Remove HTML tags and attributes using regex
        String pattern = "<[^>]+>";
        Pattern htmlPattern = Pattern.compile(pattern);

        Matcher matcher = htmlPattern.matcher(sentence);
        StringBuffer buffer = new StringBuffer();

        while (matcher.find()) {
            matcher.appendReplacement(buffer, "");
        }

        matcher.appendTail(buffer);

        return buffer.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sentence = "<p>I am learning to Code.</p>\n<code>Code is fun to learn.</code>\n<span>I love coding!</span>";
        String word = "code";

        int frequency = countWordFrequency(sentence, word);
        System.out.println("Frequency of the word \"" + word + "\" in the sentence: " + frequency);
    }
}
```

In this program, we define a `countWordFrequency` method that takes a sentence and a word as inputs and returns the frequency of the word in the sentence. 

First, we trim the sentence and word to remove any leading or trailing whitespace. Then, we remove any HTML tags and attributes from the sentence using a regex pattern. The `removeHtmlTags` method uses `Matcher.appendReplacement` and `Matcher.appendTail` to replace the matched HTML tags with an empty string.

Next, we prepare a regex pattern to find the word as a separate word. The pattern uses the `\b` boundary matcher to match the word boundaries and `Pattern.quote` to escape any special characters in the word. We compile this pattern with the `CASE_INSENSITIVE` flag to make the search case-insensitive.

We initialize the frequency variable to 0 and use a `Matcher` to find all occurrences of the word in the sentence using the prepared pattern. We increment the frequency for each match found.

In the `main` method, we define a sample sentence and word, and call the `countWordFrequency` method to get the frequency of the word. Finally, we print the frequency to the console.

