```javascript
function rotateString(inputString) {
  // Check if input string is empty
  if (inputString === "") {
    return "Error: Input string cannot be empty.";
  }

  // Generate a random rotation number between 5 and 15
  const rotationNumber = Math.floor(Math.random() * 11) + 5;

  // Check if rotation number is within the specified range
  if (rotationNumber < 5 || rotationNumber > 15) {
    return "Error: Rotation number must be between 5 and 15.";
  }

  // Rotate the string using the rotation number
  const rotatedString = inputString.slice(rotationNumber) + inputString.slice(0, rotationNumber);

  return rotatedString;
}

// Example usage
const inputString = "Hello World!";
const rotatedString = rotateString(inputString);
console.log(rotatedString);
```

This program takes an input string and checks if it is empty. If it is, it returns an error message. If not, it generates a random rotation number between 5 and 15. If the rotation number is not within the specified range, it returns an error message. Finally, it rotates the input string using the rotation number and returns the rotated string.

