Here is the program in C# that sorts an array of integers in ascending order using the Bubble Sort algorithm and tracks the number of comparisons and swaps made during the sorting process:

```csharp
using System;

class BubbleSort
{
    static int comparisons = 0;
    static int swaps = 0;

    static void BubbleSortRecursive(int[] arr, int n)
    {
        if (n == 1)
            return;

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)
        {
            if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1])
            {
                Swap(arr, i, i + 1);
            }
            comparisons++;
        }

        BubbleSortRecursive(arr, n - 1);
    }

    static void Swap(int[] arr, int i, int j)
    {
        int temp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[j];
        arr[j] = temp;
        swaps++;
    }

    static void Main()
    {
        int[] arr = { 64, 34, 25, 12, 22, 11, 90 };

        Console.WriteLine("Original Array: ");
        PrintArray(arr);

        BubbleSortRecursive(arr, arr.Length);

        Console.WriteLine("\nSorted Array: ");
        PrintArray(arr);

        Console.WriteLine("\nNumber of comparisons: " + comparisons);
        Console.WriteLine("Number of swaps: " + swaps);
    }

    static void PrintArray(int[] arr)
    {
        foreach (int num in arr)
        {
            Console.Write(num + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

In this program, we have a static variable `comparisons` and `swaps` to track the number of comparisons and swaps made during the sorting process. 

The `BubbleSortRecursive` function implements the bubble sort algorithm in a recursive manner. It swaps adjacent elements if they are in the wrong order and then recursively calls itself with `n-1` elements until the array is sorted.

The `Swap` function is used to swap two elements in the array and increments the `swaps` counter.

In the `Main` method, we define an array of integers and call the `BubbleSortRecursive` function to sort the array. After sorting, we display the sorted array, along with the total number of comparisons and swaps made during the sorting process.

