- We use a while loop to iterate until `left` is less than `right`.
- Inside the loop, we use another while loop to find the first odd number from the left side. We increment `left` until we find an odd number or until `left` becomes equal to `right`.
- Similarly, we use another while loop to find the first even number from the right side. We decrement `right` until we find an even number or until `left` becomes equal to `right`.
- Once we find an odd number at `left` and an even number at `right`, we swap them.
- We repeat this process until `left` becomes equal to `right`, which means we have partitioned the array into even and odd numbers.

This solution works by maintaining two pointers and swapping odd and even numbers. It ensures that all even numbers are placed at the beginning of the array, followed by the odd numbers.

