4. If the timezone data is not cached, it starts a Redis transaction using the `watch`, `multi`, `set`, `expire`, and `exec` methods. It stores the current default timezone (`date_default_timezone_get()`) in Redis with the specified timezone as the key. It also sets an expiry time of 1 hour (3600 seconds) for the cached data.
5. If the timezone data is already cached, it retrieves the cached data using the `get` method.
