          {id}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

export default DivList;
```

In this example, we use the `useState` hook to create a state variable called `divs` to store the current order of the divs. We generate an array of 500 unique IDs using the `generateUniqueIds` function and initialize the state with it.

The `sortDivs` function takes the selected attribute as a parameter and sorts the `divs` array accordingly. We use the `setDivs` function to update the state with the sorted array.

The `handleDivClick` function is called when a div is clicked and performs the desired manipulation based on the div's ID. In this example, it simply logs the ID to the console.

