Find the calculations of the time complexity of the following coded snippet.

for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
 for (j = i; j < n; j++) {
  for (k = j; k < n; k++) {
   for (l = k; l < n; l++) {
    console.log(i, j, k, l);
   }
  }
 }
}

In the original problem, we had three nested loops iterating from i to n, j to n, and k to n respectively. We printed out the values of i, j, and k. 

In this rewritten problem, we have added an additional nested loop iterating from k to n. We now print out the values of i, j, k, and l.

The time complexity of this code snippet can be calculated as follows:

The outermost loop runs n times.
The second loop runs (n - i) times for each iteration of the outer loop.
The third loop runs (n - j) times for each iteration of the second loop.
The innermost loop runs (n - k) times for each iteration of the third loop.

So, the total number of iterations can be calculated as follows:

Total iterations = (n) + (n - 1) + (n - 2) + ... + 1

The sum of the above series is given by the formula:

Total iterations = (n * (n + 1)) / 2

Therefore, the time complexity of this code snippet is O(n^2).

