To handle circular references, the program uses a `visited` set to keep track of objects that have already been visited. If an object has already been visited, the function `countProperties` returns 0 to break the cycle and avoid infinite recursion.

The `findLargestObject` function iterates through the properties of the given object and checks if each property is an object or array. If so, it calls `countProperties` to count the number of properties in that nested structure. If the count is greater than the current maximum number of properties, it updates the maximum number of properties and stores a reference to the object with the most properties.

