Here's a PHP program that finds the length of the longest common substring between two given strings:

```php
<?php

function findLongestCommonSubstring($string1, $string2) {
    $length1 = strlen($string1);
    $length2 = strlen($string2);

    $maxLength = 0;
    $endIndex = 0;

    $dp = array();
    for ($i = 0; $i <= $length1; $i++) {
        $dp[$i] = array();
        for ($j = 0; $j <= $length2; $j++) {
            $dp[$i][$j] = 0;
        }
    }

    for ($i = 1; $i <= $length1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 1; $j <= $length2; $j++) {
            if ($string1[$i - 1] === $string2[$j - 1]) {
                $dp[$i][$j] = $dp[$i - 1][$j - 1] + 1;
                if ($dp[$i][$j] > $maxLength) {
                    $maxLength = $dp[$i][$j];
                    $endIndex = $i - 1;
                }
            } else {
                $dp[$i][$j] = 0;
            }
        }
    }

    if ($maxLength === 0) {
        return "No common substring found.";
    }

    $longestCommonSubstrings = array();
    for ($i = $endIndex - $maxLength + 1; $i <= $endIndex; $i++) {
        $longestCommonSubstrings[] = $string1[$i];
    }

    return implode("", $longestCommonSubstrings);
}

$string1 = "abcdefgh";
$string2 = "abcpqrdef";

$longestCommonSubstring = findLongestCommonSubstring($string1, $string2);

echo "Longest common substring: " . $longestCommonSubstring . "\n";
echo "Length of longest common substring: " . strlen($longestCommonSubstring) . "\n";

?>
```

