The static method `getNextId()` allows us to access the value of `nextId` from outside the class without creating an instance of `Employee`. It can be useful for getting the next available ID or performing any logic based on the static variable.

By using static variables in this scenario, we ensure that each `Employee` object gets a unique ID without having to rely on external logic or manually managing the ID assignment.

