- Next, we check if `n` is divisible by 2. If it is, then it is not prime (except if `n` is 2, but we have already handled that case).
- We then iterate from 3 to the square root of `n`, checking if `n` is divisible by each number. If it is, then it is not prime.
- If none of the above conditions are met, then `n` is prime.

This implementation has a time complexity of O(sqrt(n)) because we iterate up to the square root of `n` to check for divisibility.

