Here is an efficient function in R that calculates the median from a given list of numbers:

```R
calculate_median <- function(numlist) {
  n <- length(numlist)
  sorted_nums <- sort(numlist)  # Sort the list in ascending order

  if (n %% 2 == 1) {
    # If the list has odd number of elements, return the middle value
    median <- sorted_nums[(n + 1) %/% 2]
  } else {
    # If the list has even number of elements, return the average of the two middle values
    median <- (sorted_nums[n %/% 2] + sorted_nums[(n %/% 2) + 1]) / 2
  }

  return(median)
}
```

