Here's a JavaScript code snippet that uses a recursive function to reverse a string, extract the last three characters, and display them in uppercase letters:

```javascript
function reverseAndExtractLastThree(str) {
  // Base case: if the string length is less than or equal to 3, return the reversed string in uppercase
  if (str.length <= 3) {
    return str.split('').reverse().join('').toUpperCase();
  }

  // Recursive case: reverse the string and extract the last three characters recursively
  return reverseAndExtractLastThree(str.slice(1)) + str.charAt(0);
}

