    }
}
```

3. Implement the addNodeAtHead method to add a node at the head of the doubly linked list. This method should take the key and value of the node as parameters and create a new node with these values. If the list is empty, the new node should become both the head and tail. Otherwise, update the next and previous references of the existing head and the new node.

```java
public void addNodeAtHead(int key, int value) {
    Node newNode = new Node(key, value);

    if (head == null) {
        head = newNode;
        tail = newNode;
    } else {
        newNode.next = head;
        head.previous = newNode;
        head = newNode;
    }
}
```

4. Implement the addNodeAtTail method to add a node at the tail of the doubly linked list. This method should take the key and value of the node as parameters and create a new node with these values. If the list is empty, the new node should become both the head and tail. Otherwise, update the next and previous references of the existing tail and the new node.

```java
public void addNodeAtTail(int key, int value) {
    Node newNode = new Node(key, value);

    if (tail == null) {
        head = newNode;
        tail = newNode;
    } else {
        newNode.previous = tail;
        tail.next = newNode;
        tail = newNode;
    }
}
```

5. Implement the removeNode method to remove a node from the doubly linked list given its key. This method should take the key as a parameter and search for a node with the matching key. If found, remove the node by updating the next and previous references of the adjacent nodes. If the node to be removed is the head or tail, update the head or tail references accordingly. If the key is not found, throw an appropriate exception.

```java
public void removeNode(int key) {
    if (head == null) {
        throw new NoSuchElementException("List is empty");
    }

    Node current = head;
    while (current != null) {
        if (current.key == key) {
            if (current == head) {
                head = current.next;
                if (head != null) {
                    head.previous = null;
                }
                if (current == tail) {
                    tail = null;
                }
            } else if (current == tail) {
                tail = current.previous;
                tail.next = null;
            } else {
                current.previous.next = current.next;
                current.next.previous = current.previous;
            }
            return;
        }
        current = current.next;
    }

    throw new NoSuchElementException("Key not found in list");
}
```

