Here is the implementation of the bubble sort algorithm in Java:

```java
public class BubbleSort {
    public static void bubbleSort(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                    // Swap arr[j] and arr[j + 1]
                    int temp = arr[j];
                    arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                    arr[j + 1] = temp;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {5, 8, 2, 7, 1, 9, 3, 6, 4, 7, 2, 1, 6};
        bubbleSort(arr);
        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(arr));
    }
}
```

The main function is used to test the bubbleSort function. We create an array `arr` with the given elements and then call the bubbleSort function to sort the array. Finally, we print the sorted array using the `Arrays.toString` method.

