print(capitalizer.string)  # Output: hello world

capitalizer.capitalize_first_letter()
print(capitalizer.string)  # Output: Hello world

capitalizer.reverse_capitalization()
print(capitalizer.string)  # Output: Hello WORLD
```

In this implementation, the `Capitalizer` class takes a string as an argument in its constructor and stores it in the `string` attribute. The `capitalize_first_letter` method capitalizes the first letter of the string by replacing the first character with its uppercase version. The `reverse_capitalization` method iterates over each character in the string and checks if it is alphabetic. If it is, it reverses its capitalization by changing it to uppercase if it was lowercase, and vice versa. The modified string is stored back in the `string` attribute.

