```java
public static boolean isPalindrome(String s) {
    // Remove spaces and punctuation, and convert to lowercase
    String cleanedString = s.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9]", "").toLowerCase();

    // Check if the cleaned string is a palindrome
    int left = 0;
    int right = cleanedString.length() - 1;
    while (left < right) {
        if (cleanedString.charAt(left) != cleanedString.charAt(right)) {
            return false;
        }
        left++;
        right--;
    }
    return true;
}
```

Explanation:
1. We first remove all spaces and punctuation from the input string using the `replaceAll()` method. We replace all characters that are not alphanumeric with an empty string.
2. We then convert the cleaned string to lowercase using the `toLowerCase()` method to make the palindrome check case-insensitive.
3. We use two pointers, `left` and `right`, to iterate through the cleaned string from both ends.
4. In each iteration, we compare the characters at the `left` and `right` positions. If they are not equal, we return `false` because the string is not a palindrome.
5. If the characters at all positions match, we return `true` because the string is a palindrome.

The time complexity of this solution is O(n), where n is the length of the input string.

