Here is a possible implementation of the 2DVector class in Java:

```java
public class Vector2D {
    private double x;
    private double y;

    public Vector2D(double x, double y) {
        this.x = x;
        this.y = y;
    }

    public double getX() {
        return x;
    }

    public double getY() {
        return y;
    }

    public void setX(double x) {
        this.x = x;
    }

    public void setY(double y) {
        this.y = y;
    }

    public double magnitude() {
        return Math.sqrt(x * x + y * y);
    }

    public double dotProduct(Vector2D other) {
        return x * other.x + y * other.y;
    }

    public double angle(Vector2D other) {
        double dot = dotProduct(other);
        double magnitudeProduct = magnitude() * other.magnitude();
        return Math.acos(dot / magnitudeProduct);
    }

    public double crossProduct(Vector2D other) {
        return x * other.y - y * other.x;
    }

    public Vector2D add(Vector2D other) {
        return new Vector2D(x + other.x, y + other.y);
    }

    public Vector2D subtract(Vector2D other) {
        return new Vector2D(x - other.x, y - other.y);
    }

    public Vector2D multiply(double scalar) {
        return new Vector2D(x * scalar, y * scalar);
    }
}
```

You can use this class to create instances of 2D vectors and perform various operations on them. Here is an example usage:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Vector2D vector1 = new Vector2D(3, 4);
        Vector2D vector2 = new Vector2D(1, 2);

        System.out.println("Vector 1: (" + vector1.getX() + ", " + vector1.getY() + ")");
        System.out.println("Vector 2: (" + vector2.getX() + ", " + vector2.getY() + ")");
        System.out.println("Magnitude of Vector 1: " + vector1.magnitude());
        System.out.println("Dot Product of Vector 1 and Vector 2: " + vector1.dotProduct(vector2));
        System.out.println("Angle between Vector 1 and Vector 2: " + vector1.angle(vector2));
        System.out.println("Cross Product of Vector 1 and Vector 2: " + vector1.crossProduct(vector2));

        Vector2D sum = vector1.add(vector2);
        System.out.println("Sum of Vector 1 and Vector 2: (" + sum.getX() + ", " + sum.getY() + ")");

        Vector2D difference = vector1.subtract(vector2);
