Here is the Java program to find the second maximum and second minimum values in an array of integers, excluding any duplicates:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;

public class SecondMinMax {

    public static void findSecondMinMax(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;

        if (n < 2) {
            System.out.println("Error: Not enough elements in the array.");
            return;
        }

        Arrays.sort(arr);

        int secondMin = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        int secondMax = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (arr[i] != arr[i - 1]) {
                secondMin = Math.min(secondMin, arr[i]);
                secondMax = Math.max(secondMax, arr[i - 1]);
            }
        }

        if (secondMin == Integer.MAX_VALUE || secondMax == Integer.MIN_VALUE) {
            System.out.println("Error: All elements in the array are duplicates.");
            return;
        }

        System.out.println("Second Minimum: " + secondMin);
        System.out.println("Second Maximum: " + secondMax);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {2, 4, 5, 3, 4, 5, 1, 1, 2, 3, 7};

        findSecondMinMax(arr);
    }
}
```

This program first checks if the array has enough elements. If not, it returns an error message. Then, it sorts the array in ascending order using the `Arrays.sort()` method. 

Next, it initializes `secondMin` and `secondMax` variables with the maximum and minimum possible values respectively. Then, it iterates over the sorted array, skipping duplicates, and updates `secondMin` and `secondMax` if necessary.

Finally, it checks if any of the variables remain unchanged, which indicates that all elements in the array are duplicates. If so, it returns an error message. Otherwise, it prints the second minimum and second maximum values.

