To find the first occurrence of a specific value in a sorted array using binary search, we can modify the binary search algorithm slightly. Instead of returning when we find a match, we continue searching to the left of the mid index to find the first occurrence.

Here is the implementation in JavaScript:

```javascript
function findFirstOccurrence(arr, target) {
  let low = 0;
  let high = arr.length - 1;
  let result = -1;

  while (low <= high) {
    let mid = Math.floor((low + high) / 2);

    if (arr[mid] === target) {
      result = mid;
      high = mid - 1; // Continue searching to the left
    } else if (arr[mid] < target) {
      low = mid + 1;
    } else {
      high = mid - 1;
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(log n) since we are dividing the search space in half with each iteration of the while loop.

Let's test the function with some sample inputs:

