The table for logging deletion activity should have the following structure:
- Table name (TEXT)
- Deletion timestamp (TIMESTAMP)

Your task is to modify the code provided below to fix the error in the "confirm_deletion()" function call and implement the logging of deletion activity.

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION delete_table(table_name TEXT) RETURNS VOID AS $$
DECLARE
    confirm BOOLEAN;
BEGIN
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_tables WHERE tablename = table_name) THEN
        RAISE NOTICE 'Table % does not exist', table_name;
        RETURN;
    END IF;

    RAISE NOTICE 'Are you sure you want to delete table %?', table_name;
    SELECT confirm_deletion() INTO confirm;

    IF confirm IS TRUE THEN
        EXECUTE 'DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ' || table_name || ' CASCADE';
        RAISE NOTICE 'Table % has been deleted', table_name;

        -- Log the deletion activity
        INSERT INTO deletion_log (table_name, deletion_timestamp)
        VALUES (table_name, NOW());
    END IF;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

Note: The "deletion_log" table mentioned above should already exist in the database.

