Here is a Java program that removes comments from a Java program, handling nested comments and scenarios where comments are within string literals or within other valid syntax elements:

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.FileWriter;
import java.io.IOException;

public class RemoveComments {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String inputFile = "input.java";  // Specify the input file name
        String outputFile = "output.java";  // Specify the output file name

        try {
            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(inputFile));
            FileWriter writer = new FileWriter(outputFile);

            String line;
            boolean insideComment = false;
            boolean insideString = false;

            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                StringBuilder stringBuilder = new StringBuilder();
                for (int i = 0; i < line.length(); i++) {
                    char currentChar = line.charAt(i);
                    if (!insideComment && !insideString && i < line.length() - 1 && line.charAt(i + 1) == '/') {
                        if (currentChar == '/') {
                            break;  // Single line comment, ignore rest of the line
                        } else if (currentChar == '*') {
                            insideComment = true;
                            i++;
                            continue;  // Start of multi-line comment, ignore next character
                        }
                    }

                    if (insideComment) {
                        if (currentChar == '*' && i < line.length() - 1 && line.charAt(i + 1) == '/') {
                            insideComment = false;
                            i++;
                        }
                    } else if (!insideString && currentChar == '"') {
                        insideString = true;
                    } else if (insideString && currentChar == '"' && line.charAt(i - 1) != '\\') {
                        insideString = false;
                    }

                    if (!insideComment) {
                        stringBuilder.append(currentChar);
                    }
                }

                if (!insideComment) {
                    writer.write(stringBuilder.toString() + "\n");
                }
            }

            reader.close();
            writer.close();

            System.out.println("Comments removed successfully!");
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

To use this program, you need to specify the input file name and the output file name in the `inputFile` and `outputFile` variables, respectively. The program reads the input file line by line and removes the comments based on the specified logic. The resulting code without comments is written to the output file.

