Here is the Java code to sort the given array [4, 9, 3, 6, 2, 1] in descending order using a bubble sort algorithm:

```java
public class BubbleSortDescending {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {4, 9, 3, 6, 2, 1};
        bubbleSortDescending(arr);
        System.out.println("Sorted array in descending order: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");
        }
    }

    public static void bubbleSortDescending(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        boolean swapped;

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            swapped = false;

            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                if (arr[j] < arr[j + 1]) {
                    int temp = arr[j];
                    arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                    arr[j + 1] = temp;
                    swapped = true;
                }
            }

            if (!swapped) {
                break;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

