Here is a Java program that implements the binary search algorithm with the specified requirements:

```java
public class BinarySearch {
    public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = arr.length - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (arr[mid] == target) {
                // Check if it is the leftmost occurrence
                while (mid > 0 && arr[mid - 1] == target) {
                    mid--;
                }
                return mid;
            }

            if (arr[mid] < target) {
                left = mid + 1;
            } else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9};
        int target = 4;

        int index = binarySearch(arr, target);

        if (index != -1) {
            System.out.println("Target found at index " + index);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Target not found in the array");
        }
    }
}
```

In this program, the `binarySearch` method takes an input array `arr` and a target integer `target`. It uses a while loop to perform the binary search on the array. The `left` and `right` variables represent the boundaries of the subarray being searched. The `mid` variable is calculated as the middle index of the subarray.

Inside the loop, the program checks if the element at the `mid` index is equal to the target integer. If it is, it then checks if it is the leftmost occurrence by iterating backwards until it finds the leftmost occurrence. If multiple occurrences of the target integer exist, the leftmost index is returned.

If the element at the `mid` index is less than the target integer, the `left` pointer is updated to `mid + 1` to continue searching the right half of the array. If it is greater, the `right` pointer is updated to `mid - 1` to search the left half.

If the target integer is not found in the array, the program returns -1.

In the `main` method, an example array `arr` and target integer `target` are provided. The `binarySearch` method is called with these parameters and the result is printed to the console.

