Here is an improved implementation of the binary search algorithm that handles duplicate elements in the array using a recursive approach:

```python
def binary_search(array, target, low, high):
  if low <= high:
    mid = (low + high) // 2
    if array[mid] == target:
      # Handle duplicates
      while mid > low and array[mid - 1] == target:
        mid -= 1
      return mid
    elif array[mid] < target:
      return binary_search(array, target, mid + 1, high)
    else:
      return binary_search(array, target, low, mid - 1)
  return -1

