tree.print_tree()

tree.delete(5)
print("\nTree after deleting 5:")
tree.print_tree()

search_result = tree.search(8)
print("\nSearch result for 8:", search_result.value)
```

This implementation uses a Node class to represent each node in the tree. The `insert()` method inserts a new value into the tree, while the `search()` method searches for a value in the tree and returns the corresponding node. The `delete()` method removes a value from the tree, and the `print_tree()` method prints the values of the tree in order.

