In this code, we first check if the input is a valid positive integer within the range of 1 to 100. If it's not, we return an error message.

If the input is valid, we use a loop to calculate the nth Fibonacci number iteratively. We start with the first two numbers of the sequence (0 and 1) and keep updating them until we reach the desired position.

The time complexity of this solution is O(n), which is more efficient than the naive recursive solution.

