Here's an example of a PHP function that removes special characters from a given string, counts the removed characters, and returns the modified string. The time complexity of this function is O(n), where n is the length of the input string.

```php
function removeSpecialCharacters($str) {
    $removedChars = array();
    $modifiedStr = '';

    for ($i = 0; $i < strlen($str); $i++) {
        $char = $str[$i];

        // Check if the character is a special character
        if (!ctype_alnum($char)) {
            // Increment the count of the removed character
            if (isset($removedChars[$char])) {
                $removedChars[$char]++;
            } else {
                $removedChars[$char] = 1;
            }
        } else {
            // Append non-special characters to the modified string
            $modifiedStr .= $char;
        }
    }

    return array(
        'removedChars' => $removedChars,
        'modifiedStr' => $modifiedStr
    );
}

