If the array is not empty, the function proceeds to sort the array using the `mergeSort` function, which is implemented with a time complexity of O(n log n). The sorted array is then used to determine the median based on the length of the array.

For arrays with an odd length, the function returns the middle value of the sorted array. For arrays with an even length, the function calculates the average of the two middle values and returns it as the median.

The `mergeSort` function is a recursive implementation of the merge sort algorithm, which splits the array into halves, sorts each half separately, and then merges the sorted halves back together.

The `merge` function is a helper function used by `mergeSort` to merge two sorted arrays into a single sorted array. It compares the elements of the two arrays and pushes the smaller element into the result array, until all elements from both arrays have been processed.

