To set up Redis, you can follow the official Redis documentation for your specific environment. Make sure to start the Redis server and ensure it's accessible by the Node.js application.

Please note that the example code assumes you have already installed the required dependencies (`express`, `axios`, `redis`). You can install them by running `npm install express axios redis`.

Make sure to replace the `weatherServiceEndpoint` and `temperatureConversionEndpoint` with the actual endpoints provided by your chosen weather service provider and temperature conversion API.

Also, keep in mind that this is a simplified example and may require further modifications and error handling based on your specific use case and the APIs you're integrating with.

