```java
public class KthSmallestElement {

    public static int findKthSmallest(int[] arr, int k) {
        if (arr.length == 0) {
            return -1;
        }
        return findKthSmallestHelper(arr, 0, arr.length - 1, k);
    }

    private static int findKthSmallestHelper(int[] arr, int left, int right, int k) {
        if (left == right) {
            return arr[left];
        }
        int pivotIndex = partition(arr, left, right);
        if (k - 1 == pivotIndex) {
            return arr[pivotIndex];
        } else if (k - 1 < pivotIndex) {
            return findKthSmallestHelper(arr, left, pivotIndex - 1, k);
        } else {
            return findKthSmallestHelper(arr, pivotIndex + 1, right, k);
        }
    }

    private static int partition(int[] arr, int left, int right) {
        int pivot = arr[right];
        int i = left - 1;
        for (int j = left; j < right; j++) {
            if (arr[j] <= pivot) {
                i++;
                swap(arr, i, j);
            }
        }
        swap(arr, i + 1, right);
        return i + 1;
    }

    private static void swap(int[] arr, int i, int j) {
        int temp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[j];
        arr[j] = temp;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {5, 2, 3, 4, 4};
        int k = 3;
        int kthSmallest = findKthSmallest(arr, k);
        System.out.println("Kth Smallest Element: " + kthSmallest);
    }
}
```

This program uses the quickselect algorithm to find the kth smallest element in an array. The `findKthSmallest()` method is the entry point to the program, which checks for the base case of an empty array and then calls the helper method `findKthSmallestHelper()`.

The `findKthSmallestHelper()` method implements the quickselect algorithm recursively. It partitions the array based on a chosen pivot, and then recursively calls itself on the appropriate partition until the kth smallest element is found. The pivot element is determined by the `partition()` method, which uses the last element as the pivot and rearranges the elements such that all elements smaller than the pivot are on its left and all elements larger are on its right.

The `swap()` method is a helper method to swap two elements in the array.

In the `main()` method, a sample input array and k value are provided to test the program. You can modify the array and k value to test different scenarios.

