Given an array of integers, write a JavaScript function to remove all duplicate elements while maintaining the original order of the array. Your implementation should have a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the array.

For example, given the input array [1, 2, 3, 2, 1, 4, 5], the function should return [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]. The duplicate elements 2 and 1 have been removed, while the original order of the remaining elements is maintained.

You can assume that the input array will only contain positive integers. You can use any built-in JavaScript methods or data structures to solve this problem.

**Erroneous Code**

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(array) {
  let result = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
    if (!result.includes(array[i])) {
      result.push(array[i]);
    }
  }
  return result;
}
