The error in the code is that the `includes` method has a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the `result` array. This means that the overall time complexity of the solution is not O(n), as required.

To fix this error and achieve the desired time complexity, we can use a `Set` data structure to keep track of the unique elements. We can iterate over the input array and add each element to the `Set` if it is not already present. Finally, we can convert the `Set` back to an array to maintain the original order.

Here is the corrected code:

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(array) {
  let uniqueElements = new Set();
  let result = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
