```java
public class LowercaseStringConverter {
    public static String convertToLowerCase(String input) {
        // Remove leading and trailing white spaces
        int start = 0;
        int end = input.length() - 1;

        while (start <= end && Character.isWhitespace(input.charAt(start))) {
            start++;
        }

        while (end >= start && Character.isWhitespace(input.charAt(end))) {
            end--;
        }

        // Convert remaining characters to lowercase
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {
            char c = input.charAt(i);
            if (c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z') {
                c = (char) (c + 32); // Convert uppercase to lowercase
            }
            result.append(c);
        }

        return result.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "   HeLLo, WoRld!   ";
        System.out.println(convertToLowerCase(input)); // Output: "hello, world!"
    }
}
```

In this function, we first remove the leading and trailing white spaces from the input string using two `while` loops. We start from the beginning and end of the string, and increment/decrement the indices until we find a non-whitespace character.

Then, we use a `StringBuilder` to construct the result string. We iterate over the remaining characters (after removing leading and trailing white spaces) and convert any uppercase letters to lowercase by adding 32 to their ASCII values.

Finally, we return the result as a string.

The time complexity of this function is O(n) because we iterate over the characters of the string only once.

