class MyClass implements Cloneable {
    private int number;

    public MyClass(int number) {
        this.number = number;
    }

    public int getNumber() {
        return number;
    }

    public void setNumber(int number) {
        this.number = number;
    }

    @Override
    public Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}

public class ArrayClone {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        MyClass[] originalArray = {new MyClass(1), new MyClass(2), new MyClass(3)};

        MyClass[] clonedArray = cloneArray(originalArray);

        // Print the cloned array elements
        for (MyClass obj : clonedArray) {
            System.out.println(obj.getNumber());
        }
    }

    public static <T extends Cloneable> T[] cloneArray(T[] originalArray) {
        // Check if all objects implement the Cloneable interface
        for (T obj : originalArray) {
            if (!(obj instanceof Cloneable)) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Object does not implement Cloneable");
            }
        }

        // Create a new array for the cloned objects
        T[] clonedArray = (T[]) new Object[originalArray.length];

        try {
            // Clone each object and add it to the cloned array
            for (int i = 0; i < originalArray.length; i++) {
                clonedArray[i] = (T) originalArray[i].clone();
            }
        } catch (CloneNotSupportedException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }

        return clonedArray;
    }
}
```

In this program, the `MyClass` class implements the `Cloneable` interface by overriding the `clone()` method. The `cloneArray()` method takes an array of objects as input and checks if each object implements the `Cloneable` interface using the `instanceof` operator. If any object does not implement the interface, an `IllegalArgumentException` is thrown.

Then, a new array is created to store the cloned objects. Each object in the original array is cloned using the `clone()` method and added to the cloned array. Finally, the cloned array is returned.

In the `main()` method, an array of `MyClass` objects is created and passed to the `cloneArray()` method. The cloned array is then printed to verify the cloning process.

